{
  "title": "Mouths",
  "about": "One huge cartoon mouth fills the wall and acts its heart out: a grin, a smirk, a Cheshire-wide sinister grin, a yell down to the uvula, a belly laugh, a gasp, a grimace, a pout, tongue out, a lip bite, a snarl, belting, an anime nervous wobble, springing from one to the next on the bar. The jaw pumps on the kick, the opening lip-syncs to the mids with consonants flicked on the hats, and heavy low end, above all the drop, pulls it into a filthy bass face. Drawn in anime, rubber-hose cartoon, grotesque detail or Lichtenstein pop art; A Hit is the jaw and the bob, B Move the consonants and sway, C Change the exaggeration and the background swell.",
